// All the levels. Coordinates are block cells: x = east, y = tier, z = south.
//
// Levels 1-10 list their pieces by hand:
// pieces: [type, x, y, z, rotation, options]
//   rotation turns the piece in 90° steps (0 = as drawn in pieces.js, 1 = 90° clockwise seen from above).
//   Dead ends, goals and plates are open to the west at rotation 0 (1 = north, 2 = east, 3 = south).
//   Curves join west+north at 0 (1 = north+east, 2 = east+south, 3 = south+west).
//   T-junctions open west+east+north at 0 (1 = north+south+east, 2 = east+west+south, 3 = south+north+west).
//   Ramps start high on the west and end low two cells east at 0; rotation 1 runs north to south.
// blocks: extra plain blocks [x, y, z], only where needed to hold the machine together.
//   Raised pieces get their support columns automatically.
//
// Levels 11 onwards are drawn instead (see grid.js for what each character means):
// map: one list of rows per tier, ground tier first. North is the top row, east is to the right.
// bands: goals that also open gates, e.g. { blue: 'A' }.
//
// Every level:
// marbles: [{ color, at: [x, y, z] }]; a marble on a dead end, goal or plate starts at its closed end.
// solution: the reference run used by the tests and to set the timers.
// traps: wrong move sequences the level is designed to punish; the tests check they fail.

